nt":10},{"name":"能源/電力","count":1},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-24","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1039684/000103968426000006/oke-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"We are incorporated under the laws of the state of Oklahoma, and our common stock is listed on the NYSE under the trading symbol \"OKE.\" We deliver energy products and services vital to an advancing world. We are a leading midstream service provider of gathering, processing, fractionation, transportation, storage and marine export services. As one of the largest integrated energy infrastructure companies in North America, we are delivering energy that makes a difference in the lives of people in the U.S. and around the world. Through our approximately 60,000-mile pipeline network, we transport the natural gas, NGLs, Refined Products and crude oil that help meet domestic and international energy demand, contribute to energy security and provide safe, reliable and responsible energy solutions needed today and into the future.","zh":null},{"en":"The midstream value chain is a vital part of the energy industry. After crude oil and natural gas are produced from upstream wells, we use our extensive infrastructure to process and transport these raw materials, readying them for end use. For transportation of crude oil, natural gas, Refined Products and NGLs, pipelines are generally the most reliable, lowest cost, least carbon intensive and safest alternative for intermediate and long-haul movements between markets and end users.","zh":null},{"en":"EnLink Acquisition - On January 31, 2025, we completed the EnLink Acquisition. Pursuant to the EnLink Merger Agreement, each publicly held common unit of EnLink was exchanged for a fixed ratio of 0.1412 shares of ONEOK common stock, including EnLink Units that were exchanged for all previously outstanding Series B Preferred Units immediately prior to closing. We issued 41 million shares of common stock with a fair value of $4.0 billion as of the closing date of the EnLink Acquisition. EnLink is now a wholly owned subsidiary.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Transportation services - Our regulated natural gas transportation services contracts are based upon rates stated in the respective tariffs, which have generally been established through shipper specific negotiation, discounts and negotiated settlements. The rates are filed with FERC or the appropriate state jurisdictional agencies. In addition, customers typically are assessed fees, such as a commodity charge, and we may retain a percentage of natural gas in-kind for our compression services. Our transportation earnings are primarily fee-based and utilize the following types of contracts:","zh":null}],"competition":[],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Natural Gas Liquids","val":16010000000,"zh":"Natural Gas Liquids"},{"name":"Refined Products & Crude Oil","val":13039000000,"zh":"Refined Products & Crude Oil"},{"name":"Natural Gas Gathering & Processing","val":7684000000,"zh":"Natural Gas Gathering & Processing"},{"name":"Wholly Owned Interstate Natural Gas Pipelines","val":1846000000,"zh":"Wholly Owned Interstate Natural Gas Pipelines"}],"total":33629000000},"prod":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Liquids Commodity","val":30408000000,"zh":"Liquids Commodity"},{"name":"Commodity Sales","val":28878000000,"zh":"Commodity Sales"},{"name":"Services","val":4751000000,"zh":"服務"},{"name":"Residue Natural Gas Sales","val":3372000000,"zh":"Residue Natural Gas Sales"},{"name":"Transportationand Storage Revenue","val":3160000000,"zh":"Transportationand Storage Revenue"},{"name":"Exchange Services & Natural Gas Gathering & Processing Revenue","val":1473000000,"zh":"Exchange Services & Natural Gas Gathering & Processing Revenue"},{"name":"Other","val":166000000,"zh":"其他"}],"total":33629000000}},"peers":["WMB","KMI","EPD","ENB","MPLX"]}}